# In S26–S37 "go beyond" is about outdoing in a craft (tuning strings, prescribing). In S1, S39 and S42 it is the unjust man's grasping for more gain or advantage.
# A3 and A4 read it in the craft sense taken from C1 and C2, so I left them with the first sense.
# "like" in P3 (S7) versus C (S44) may slide between resembling in one trait and being of the same kind. I judged this a weakness in the premise rather than a change of sense, so I marked it one.
